2026-10-19: the graded set is now on the POD 128-coordinate board (7ab74388f). A3 mf envelope distance (0.05-1.05 s) to the matching recording channel:
- 11.3 dB bass side, 13.3 dB treble side, 10.7 dB at the default point;
- on the pivoted board it was 11.8 / 13.4 / 7.7;
- the real mic-vs-mic distance is 8.4 dB.
The default point is no longer clearly better than the near-field points, so the near-field argument in this bead rests on the first-150-ms pattern (10.8 / 13.5 / 11.4 dB) and on the plate/lid physics, not on the envelope gap.

description:
## What

`percussion`'s radiation sweep (crates/fs-couple/examples/percussion/stereo.rs) solves its 4N+1 frequency samples
one after another on one core. Each sample owns its quadrature, dense matrix and LU, and the loop only places values
by index and folds order-independent min/max diagnostics. So the samples can run on several threads with
bit-identical results and the same first refusal.

Patch (151 lines, applies to origin/main 708f9882d; the stereo.rs anchors are unchanged since 9fa109fd1):
inline at the end of this description.
- `FRANKENSIM_BEM_THREADS` sets the thread count. The default is 1, which is exactly the serial loop.
- The highest frequency is still solved first and alone, so the wavelength guard refuses an underresolved band before
  any other work.
- The remaining samples run in contiguous descending chunks on `std::thread::scope` (fs-exec's crew would do as well).
  Each chunk stops at its own first refusal.
- The merge walks the serial order, so the refusal it returns is the one the serial loop would have returned.
- The example's `Error` is not Send, so a refusal crosses threads as its message.

## Why

A QuarterTone final drum render (music_theory_data_tool, job 21c2f8b1) runs the hi-hats on the far-field reciprocal
receiver: paired shells, 3072 unknowns, 24 intervals at order 12, so 97 samples and 1.32e13 sweep work units. On trj
at load 150-190 they ran single-threaded for 22.5 h and are still running.
- The same nine renders with `FRANKENSIM_BEM_THREADS=10` take about 8 cores each.
- The 1536-unknown verify case's 17-sample sweep finished in 27 min with 8 threads.

## Proof

Measured on trj 2026-10-16 (load 150-190 on 128 cores). The patched binary is 33c86971e + the frankensim-dxb6z
completions + this patch, sha256 da3080b7355ccfff..., built through rch on vmi1227854. The original is the QuarterTone
kit binary a2ccf4c98193be53.
- verify case: a crash16 far-field reciprocal render, 40..300 Hz, 4 intervals at order 2 (17 samples, 1536 unknowns),
  run by the original binary, the patched binary on 1 thread and the patched binary on 8 threads.
  - All three exit 1, and their stderr is byte-identical (md5 49fd09d87bb3...). That includes the observer fit's refusal:
    holdout max=0.13493764308808967, rms=0.10385150747678049. The fit computes those from every sweep sample.
  - The WAV leg is vacuous: all three refused before writing audio.
  - Wall time: 8 threads 27 min for the sweep, the serial original ~2.9 h.
- A non-vacuous check is running: the kit crash (24 intervals at order 12, 97 samples) re-rendered with 10 threads,
  compared byte for byte with the original binary's WAV (sha256 900ea4f4b6666b70..., 8.8 h serial). The result
  follows as a comment.

## Notes

- Memory grows with threads: each one holds a dense matrix plus LU, about 150 MB per thread at 3072 complex unknowns.
- The patch was built against 33c86971e plus the frankensim-dxb6z completions, because committed percussion does
  not compile (frankensim-dxb6z).

## The patch (origin/main 708f9882d)

```diff
--- a/crates/fs-couple/examples/percussion/stereo.rs
+++ b/crates/fs-couple/examples/percussion/stereo.rs
@@ -180,56 +180,105 @@
         omega[omega.len()-1]/medium.sound_speed,spec,count,omega.len(),gate)?)}else{None};
     let reciprocal_observations=reciprocal.as_ref().map(|source|observations.reciprocal(source,gate)).transpose()?;
     let mut maximum_backward_residual=0.0_f64;let mut maximum_flux_defect=0.0_f64;
-    // Solve the highest frequency first: the BEM owner's wavelength guard can
-    // reject an underresolved band before spending work on its lower samples.
-    for index in (0..omega.len()).rev() {
-        if gate.is_requested() {return Err("radiation preparation cancelled".into());}
-        let w=omega[index];let k=w/medium.sound_speed;
-        let fields=acceleration_fields(&refined.weights,w);
-        let field_refs:Vec<&[C64]>=fields.iter().map(Vec::as_slice).collect();
-        if let Some(geometry)=&reciprocal {
-            // A close/directional receiver integrates the full P1/P0 field,
-            // shared across all sources. Invalid quadrature refuses cold.
-            let observation=reciprocal_observations.as_ref().ok_or("missing reciprocal receiver scene")?.prepare(k,gate)?;
-            let solutions=geometry.solve_batch(k,medium,&field_refs,||gate.is_requested())?;
+    // Each frequency sample owns its quadrature, matrix and LU; the loop below
+    // only places values by index and folds order-independent min/max
+    // diagnostics, so FRANKENSIM_BEM_THREADS (default 1, the serial loop) may
+    // solve the samples on several threads: the same numbers, the same first
+    // refusal. The highest frequency still goes first, alone: the BEM owner's
+    // wavelength guard can reject an underresolved band before spending work
+    // on its lower samples.
+    struct Sample {values:Vec<Vec<C64>>,ppw:f64,condition:f64,residual:f64,flux:f64,impedance:Option<Vec<C64>>}
+    let solve=|index:usize|->Result<Sample,String> {
+        let run=||->Result<Sample,Error> {
+            if gate.is_requested() {return Err("radiation preparation cancelled".into());}
+            let w=omega[index];let k=w/medium.sound_speed;
+            let fields=acceleration_fields(&refined.weights,w);
+            let field_refs:Vec<&[C64]>=fields.iter().map(Vec::as_slice).collect();
+            let mut sample=Sample {values:vec![vec![C64::new(0.0,0.0);count];receivers.len()],ppw:f64::INFINITY,
+                condition:0.0,residual:0.0,flux:0.0,impedance:None};
+            if let Some(geometry)=&reciprocal {
+                // A close/directional receiver integrates the full P1/P0 field,
+                // shared across all sources. Invalid quadrature refuses cold.
+                let observation=reciprocal_observations.as_ref().ok_or("missing reciprocal receiver scene")?.prepare(k,gate)?;
+                let solutions=geometry.solve_batch(k,medium,&field_refs,||gate.is_requested())?;
+                for (input,solution) in solutions.iter().enumerate() {
+                    sample.ppw=sample.ppw.min(solution.panels_per_wavelength);
+                    sample.residual=sample.residual.max(solution.backward_residual);
+                    sample.flux=sample.flux.max(solution.flux_balance);
+                    for channel in 0..receivers.len() {
+                        if gate.is_requested() {return Err("reciprocal observation cancelled".into());}
+                        sample.values[channel][input]=observation.response(channel,solution)?;
+                    }
+                }
+                if load {
+                    let traces:Vec<&[C64]>=solutions.iter().map(|s|s.pressure.as_slice()).collect();
+                    sample.impedance=Some(feedback::project_pressures(&surface,&refined.weights,&traces,w)?);
+                }
+                return Ok(sample);
+            }
+            // Independent bounded receiver quadrature, prepared ONCE per frequency.
+            let observation=observations.prepare(k,gate)?;
+            // Geometry, factorization and all source-mode solves are independent of
+            // the observation point. Do not repeat them per microphone.
+            let solutions=if let Some(prepared)=&geometry {
+                prepared.solve_batch(k,medium,&field_refs)?
+            }else{solve_radiation_batch(&surface,k,medium,&field_refs,formulation)?};
+            if solutions.len()!=count {return Err("BEM source batch lost a mechanical input".into());}
             for (input,solution) in solutions.iter().enumerate() {
-                ppw=ppw.min(solution.panels_per_wavelength);
-                maximum_backward_residual=maximum_backward_residual.max(solution.backward_residual);
-                maximum_flux_defect=maximum_flux_defect.max(solution.flux_balance);
+                if !solution.radiated_power_roundoff_interval.1.is_finite()
+                    || !solution.panels_per_wavelength.is_finite()
+                    || !solution.condition_lower_bound.is_finite()
+                    || negative_beyond_solve_floor(solution) {
+                    return Err(format!("BEM reports invalid diagnostics or negative radiation power beyond roundoff at {} Hz, input {input}, formulation {formulation:?}: power_interval={:?}, panels_per_wavelength={}, condition_lower_bound={}; refine the acoustic solve",
+                        w/core::f64::consts::TAU,solution.radiated_power_roundoff_interval,
+                        solution.panels_per_wavelength,solution.condition_lower_bound).into());
+                }
+                sample.ppw=sample.ppw.min(solution.panels_per_wavelength);
+                sample.condition=sample.condition.max(solution.condition_lower_bound);
                 for channel in 0..receivers.len() {
-                    if gate.is_requested() {return Err("reciprocal observation cancelled".into());}
-                    values[channel][input][index]=observation.response(channel,solution)?;
+                    sample.values[channel][input]=observation.response(channel,solution)?;
                 }
             }
-            if load {
-                let traces:Vec<&[C64]>=solutions.iter().map(|s|s.pressure.as_slice()).collect();
-                impedances[index]=feedback::project_pressures(&surface,&refined.weights,&traces,w)?;
+            if load {sample.impedance=Some(feedback::project(&surface,&refined.weights,&solutions,w)?);}
+            Ok(sample)
+        };
+        // The example's Error is not Send; a refusal crosses threads as its message.
+        run().map_err(|error|error.to_string())
+    };
+    let threads=std::env::var("FRANKENSIM_BEM_THREADS").ok().and_then(|v|v.parse::<usize>().ok()).filter(|&n|n>0).unwrap_or(1);
+    let order:Vec<usize>=(0..omega.len()).rev().collect();
+    let mut results:Vec<Option<Result<Sample,String>>>=(0..omega.len()).map(|_|None).collect();
+    if let Some((&first,rest))=order.split_first() {
+        let head=solve(first);let refused=head.is_err();results[first]=Some(head);
+        if !refused {
+            if threads<=1 || rest.len()<=1 {
+                for &index in rest {let r=solve(index);let refused=r.is_err();results[index]=Some(r);if refused {break;}}
+            }else{
+                let chunk=rest.len().div_ceil(threads);
+                let solve=&solve;
+                let parts:Vec<Vec<(usize,Result<Sample,String>)>>=std::thread::scope(|scope| {
+                    let handles:Vec<_>=rest.chunks(chunk).map(|part|scope.spawn(move|| {
+                        let mut out=Vec::with_capacity(part.len());
+                        for &index in part {let r=solve(index);let refused=r.is_err();out.push((index,r));if refused {break;}}
